  "title": "From Fragmented to Real-Time: Rebuilding a Marketplace That Moves at the Speed of Demand",
  "summary": "Nabis rebuilt its B2B cannabis marketplace on real-time data replication via Kafka, replacing batch-synced systems that couldn't keep pace with inventory changes across California and New York. The result: accurate reorders, faster search, and a multi-cart experience for retailers managing multiple licensed locations — all updating in milliseconds.",
